      <Desc>SAN DIEGO COOPERATIVE CHARTER SCHOOL SDCCS: OPERATION OF A PUBLIC CHARTER SCHOOL FOR STUDENTS IN GRADES K-8 AT THE ORGANIZATION'S LINDA VISTA AND MOUNTAIN VIEW CAMPUSES. CONSTRUCTIVSM IS THE EDUCATIONAL PHILOSOPHY. THE SCHOOL'S UNIQUE TEACHING METHOD PROVIDES EDUCATION TO STUDENTS THROUGH EXPLORATION, REASONING AND DISCUSSION. SAN DIEGO COOPERATIVE CHARTER SCHOOL IS DISTINCTIVE FOR ITS SMALL CLASS SIZES, THE GROWING DIVERSITY OF THE FACULTY AND STUDENTS, THE HIGH QUALITY OF ITS TEACHERS, A CARING AND NURTURING ENVIRONMENT, AND THE STRENGTH OF ITS CURRICULUM. THE SCHOOL'S GOAL FOR EACH STUDENT IS ALWAYS THE SAME: TO PROVIDE SIGNIFICANT EXPERIENCES THAT WILL BEGIN A LIFELONG PROCESS OF DICOVERY LEADING TO A RICHLY REWARDING AND HAPPY LIFE.</Desc>
      <ProgSrvcAccomActy2Grp>
        <Desc>OPERATION OF AN EXTENDED DAY PROGRAM EDP TO OFFER A QUALITY BEFORE AND AFTER SCHOOL CHILDCARE PROGRAM THAT IS BASED ON THE SAME COOPERATIVE PHILOSOPHY EMPLOYED BY THE CHARTER SCHOOL, WHICH PROVIDES A SAFE, SUPPORTIVE ENVIRONMENT AND ENCOURAGES PARENT PARTICIPATION. EDP IS A HIGH QUALITY, WELL-SUPERVISED PROGRAM WHICH OFFERS A BALANCE OF ACTIVITIES DESIGNED TO DEVELOP SELF-ESTEEM AND PROVIDES A CREATIVE EDUCATIONAL AND RECREATIONAL EXPERIENCE FOR CHILDREN.</Desc>
      </ProgSrvcAccomActy2Grp>
